# Audit results and detailed explanations, part L (q661-q674). Format: see explain_a.py.
E = {}
def e(qid, stem, exp, opts=None, q=None):
    E[qid] = dict(stem=stem, exp=exp, opts=opts, q=q)

e("q661", "After an accident at work, the first step is usually", "People come first. After an accident, check how badly anyone is hurt and get help, whether first aid, a trained responder or 911 for serious injuries. Paperwork, cleanup and figuring out what happened come after the injured person is cared for.")
e("q662", "Why should a near-miss accident be reported", "A near miss reveals a hazard, like a slippery floor or loose shelf, that happened not to hurt anyone this time. Reporting it lets the company fix the problem before the next incident causes a real injury. Many serious accidents are preceded by near misses.")
e("q663", "Dividing cash-handling duties so one person counts cash", "When one person counts cash and another records deposits, no single employee controls the whole process, so stealing and hiding it would require two people working together. Segregating duties is a basic security precaution against employee theft.")
e("q664", "Comparing price, quality and delivery terms from several", "Bid analysis compares offers from several suppliers on price, quality, delivery time and terms, so the purchaser chooses the best overall value, not just the lowest price. Inventory shrinkage is loss of inventory, and depreciation is an asset's decline in value.")
e("q665", "How can employees help control a company's expenses", "Employees control expenses through everyday habits: using supplies carefully, avoiding waste, protecting equipment and following cost-saving policies. Ordering extras, ignoring procedures or working slowly to earn overtime all raise costs.")
e("q666", "For many service businesses, the largest expense employees", "In service businesses like banks and accounting firms, payroll is usually the largest expense, since the 'product' is people's work. Employees help control it by working productively, managing time well and avoiding unnecessary overtime. Raw materials matter more in manufacturing.")
e("q667", "Which practice best protects a company's sensitive digital", "Encryption scrambles data so only people with the right key can read it. Even if files are stolen or a laptop is lost, the information stays unreadable. Emailing passwords, using public computers and skipping security updates all expose data.")
e("q668", "To protect its brand name and logo from being copied", "A trademark legally protects brand names, logos and slogans that identify a company's products, so competitors can't copy them. Patents protect inventions, not names. Registering with the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office strengthens that protection.")
e("q669", "A project manager's key role is to", "A project manager plans the work, including tasks, schedule and budget, and mobilizes the people and resources needed to complete it, coordinating the team and communicating with stakeholders. They lead and coordinate rather than doing every task personally.")
e("q670", "The operations function of a business focuses on", "Operations is the function that transforms inputs, such as materials, labor, information and equipment, into the goods and services customers buy. In a bank that means processing transactions and delivering services. Advertising is marketing, and tax law comes from government.")
e("q671", "Exchanging purchase orders and invoices electronically", "Electronic data interchange (EDI) lets companies' computer systems exchange business documents like purchase orders and invoices automatically in a standard format, with no paper or retyping. That speeds transactions and reduces errors.")
e("q672", "Using computer software to plan the materials needed", "Material requirements planning (MRP) software uses production schedules and inventory levels to calculate which materials are needed, in what quantities and when. That prevents shortages and avoids tying up cash in excess inventory. CRM manages customers, not materials.")
e("q673", "One of the first steps in planning a project is to", "Identifying stakeholders, everyone affected by or able to influence the project, is one of the first planning steps, together with defining purpose and scope. Their needs and expectations shape goals, scope and communication. Final reports and closing accounts happen at the end.")
e("q674", "When evaluating project success, a team should focus", "A project's success should be judged on the measures that matter for that specific project, usually the goals, deadline, budget and quality standards set at the start. Meeting length or another project's metrics don't show whether this project achieved its purpose.")
